  <notes date="2026-07-08" rigor="FULL" model-tier="opus">
    <summary>
      Migrated CreateWorkAssignmentWizard's "Next Steps" onto the shared WizardFollowOns
      module. NextStepsSelectionStep replaced by config-driven FollowOnGrid + a
      FollowOnCardConfig[] (Assign Work / Send Email / Create an Event). The Send Email
      step body swapped from the CreateRecordWizard-owned SendEmailStep fork to the shared
      SendEmailFollowOnStep. workAssignmentService.ts is byte-for-byte unchanged.
    </summary>

    <files-changed>
      <file action="modified">.../CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/WorkAssignmentWizardDialog.tsx —
        NextStepsSelectionStep -> FollowOnGrid; removed the hand-rolled dynamic-step
        add/remove useEffect + prevSelectedActionsRef (FollowOnGrid now drives
        addDynamicStep/removeDynamicStep at click-time); added followOnCards
        FollowOnCardConfig[]; Send Email card renders shared SendEmailFollowOnStep;
        dropped import of CreateRecordWizard/steps/SendEmailStep and the WA_FOLLOW_ON_*
        maps; added a reset-time cleanup that removes any leftover follow-on dynamic
        steps on reopen (parity with the old selection-diff cleanup — the shell's own
        reset only re-homes to step 0, it does not trim injected steps).</file>
      <file action="modified">.../CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/index.ts — removed
        NextStepsSelectionStep + INextStepsSelectionStepProps exports and the dead
        WA_FOLLOW_ON_STEP_ID_MAP / _STEP_LABEL_MAP / _CANONICAL_ORDER re-exports.</file>
      <file action="modified">.../CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/formTypes.ts — removed the
        now-dead WA_FOLLOW_ON_STEP_ID_MAP / _STEP_LABEL_MAP / _CANONICAL_ORDER constants
        (replaced by a pointer comment; step ids now derived via followOnStepId()).</file>
      <file action="deleted">.../CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/NextStepsSelectionStep.tsx (git rm).</file>
      <file action="unchanged">.../CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/workAssignmentService.ts —
        VERIFIED byte-for-byte unchanged (git diff empty). Canonical ADR-024 reference.</file>
      <file action="retained">.../CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/AssignWorkStep.tsx and
        CreateFollowOnEventStep.tsx — KEPT (documented exception, see adr-tension).</file>
    </files-changed>

    <adr-tension resolution-path="A" needs="owner-ratification">
      <title>POML step 2 says delete AssignWorkStep.tsx + CreateFollowOnEventStep.tsx, but the
        shared WizardFollowOns steps are contract-incompatible with the unchangeable service.</title>
      <detail>
        The shared AssignWorkFollowOnStep and CreateEventFollowOnStep are the CreateRecordWizard
        follow-ons that CREATE CHILD records: AssignWorkFollowOnStep collects a new
        sprk_workassignment (name/description/matterType/practiceArea/priority/responseDueDate/
        attorney/paralegal/outsideCounsel) with NO lawFirmAttorney and NO notifyResources;
        CreateEventFollowOnStep produces ICreateEventFormState (eventTypeId, regardingRecordId,
        dueDate). CreateWorkAssignmentWizard's local steps have DIFFERENT semantics that feed the
        canonical, UNCHANGEABLE workAssignmentService: AssignWorkStep populates resource lookups
        (attorney/paralegal/lawFirm/lawFirmAttorney/notify) ON the WA being created via
        createWorkAssignment(...assignWork: IAssignWorkState); CreateFollowOnEventStep feeds
        createFollowOnEvent(waId, ICreateFollowOnEventState) (eventDescription/eventPriority/
        eventFinalDueDate/assignedToId). Swapping to the shared steps would require EITHER
        changing the service (forbidden — criterion #2 + orchestrator hard rule) OR changing
        follow-on fields/behavior (violates criterion #3). Per CLAUDE.md §6.5 + §11 this is a
        Path A (project-scoped exception): the two wizard-specific local step BODIES are retained;
        only the genuinely-duplicated surfaces (Next-Steps grid + Send Email) were consolidated.
        This matches the WizardFollowOns barrel's own stated target: "the four duplicated
        Next-Steps / SendEmail implementations" (it does NOT claim to unify AssignWork/CreateEvent
        across all wizards). Inlining the two bodies to satisfy a literal "delete" would be pure
        churn (relocating, not removing, the code) with regression risk and zero reuse benefit.
      </detail>
      <recommendation>Ratify Path A. If instead the owner wants zero local follow-on step files,
        that requires either extending the shared steps to carry IAssignWorkState /
        ICreateFollowOnEventState (a WizardFollowOns change, out of this task's scope) or a
        service change (forbidden). Neither is done here.</recommendation>
    </adr-tension>

    <acceptance-verification>
      <criterion id="1" status="met-with-exception">NextStepsSelectionStep local copy removed
        (grep clean) and Send Email migrated to shared. AssignWorkStep/CreateFollowOnEventStep
        retained under the documented Path-A exception above (service-coupled, not duplicates of
        the shared steps).</criterion>
      <criterion id="2" status="met">workAssignmentService.ts byte-for-byte unchanged
        (git diff --stat empty).</criterion>
      <criterion id="3" status="met">Behavior preserved: same 3 cards/icons/descriptions,
        same canAdvance gates (Send Email requires To+Subject+Body; Create Event requires
        eventName), same finish-handler actions.includes('assign-work'|'send-email'|'create-event')
        ids, canonical order (assign-work, send-email, create-event) preserved via card-array
        order, reset cleanup replicated. All 6 pre-existing tests in
        __tests__/workAssignmentService.cascade.test.ts pass.</criterion>
    </acceptance-verification>

    <build-test>tsc build (npm run build) clean. jest CreateWorkAssignmentWizard: 6/6 pass.
      eslint: 0 errors; 3 warnings all pre-existing (exhaustive-deps on the container-resolution
